    "date": 1778257317,
    "caption": "🚀A closed Building Unicorns workshop with Uri Levine - entrepreneur, investor, and co-founder of Waze and Moovit was held at Almaty Hub.\n\nThe session was organized for scale-stage startups: teams that have already passed the early stage of development, have a product and market, and are ready for the next phase of growth.\n\nThe main value of the workshop was its highly practical format: Uri Levine reviewed each startup individually. Participants shared their projects, current challenges, growth opportunities, and the barriers they face while scaling. In return, they received direct feedback, specific recommendations, and insights from an entrepreneur who has built global technology companies himself.\n\nUri Levine placed special emphasis on his key principle: fall in love with the problem, not the solution. According to him, the journey toward building a strong technology company begins with a deep understanding of the problem.\n\n💫Almaty Hub continues to create opportunities for startups that are ready to scale, go beyond local markets, and build technology companies with global potential.",
